    "passage": "With the rise of the internet, most newsstands (报刊亭) have disappeared. However, one newsstand still stands in Shanghai.\n“I ___1___ newspapers for about 38 years,” said Jiang Jun, a 67-year-old man. “There are still a number of readers with the habit of reading ___2___ and magazines. This is why I continue working at the newsstand. I open my shop before 6 a. m. ___3___ work until after 6 p. m. every day. I’d like ___4___ them.”\nJiang said that his customers are not just the elderly. Many young readers come to choose newspapers and magazines for ___5___. Chen Zaixuan, a 16-year-old school student, takes a bus ride of more than ___6___ hour every week to visit the newsstand. He prefers magazines on natural science and literature. He has kept the habit ___7___ 2024.\nAnother primary school student often visits the newsstand with his father. “The newsstand ___8___ encourage my child to read more. Most importantly, it also helps him spend ___9___ time on screens than before and learn more about the world. It is very positive for his ___10___,” said the father.\nThe newsstand is not just a shop. It brings people together and has great cultural value for the city.",
    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\">With the rise of the internet, most newsstands (报刊亭) have disappeared. However, one newsstand still stands in Shanghai.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">“I <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> newspapers for about 38 years,” said Jiang Jun, a 67-year-old man. “There are still a number of readers with the habit of reading <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;2&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> and magazines. This is why I continue working at the newsstand. I open my shop before 6 a. m. <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> work until after 6 p. m. every day. I’d like <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> them.”</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Jiang said that his customers are not just the elderly. Many young readers come to choose newspapers and magazines for <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>. Chen Zaixuan, a 16-year-old school student, takes a bus ride of more than <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;6&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> hour every week to visit the newsstand. He prefers magazines on natural science and literature. He has kept the habit <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;7&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> 2024.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Another primary school student often visits the newsstand with his father. “The newsstand <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;8&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> encourage my child to read more. Most importantly, it also helps him spend <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;9&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> time on screens than before and learn more about the world. It is very positive for his <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;10&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>,” said the father.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">The newsstand is not just a shop. It brings people together and has great cultural value for the city.</span></p>",
