    "passageHtml": "<div style=\"overflow:hidden\"><img src=\"assets/images/jr_gram8b_4_1.svg\" alt=\"Dr Bek examining a patient\"><p><span class=\"ind\">Saulebek Kabylbekov is from Kazakhstan. Now, he serves as <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> eye doctor in Daqing, China and is called Dr Bek by the locals.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\"><u>&nbsp;&nbsp;2&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> did Dr Bek first come to China? In 1993, he first came to China for a short medical trip. Five years later, he joined the Daqing Eye Hospital <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> never left. “At first, I never imagined I’d stay here this long. But over time, I found <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> growing with the hospital. Now, China is my <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> home,” the doctor said.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Dr Bek helps people deal with eye illnesses in the hospital. Sometimes, he goes to faraway villages <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;6&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> more people in need. And he is glad to pass on (传递) his skills and knowledge to young doctors to help them improve.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">With his excellent skills and smile, Dr Bek is very popular among his <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;7&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>. Liu Yanfang is one of them. The woman shared, “Over ten years ago, there was something wrong with my eyes. <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;8&nbsp;&nbsp;</u>, I met Dr Bek. He not only gave me the proper medical care, but also encouraged me to face the difficulties bravely. This year, when my eyes hurt again, I didn’t go <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;9&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> else. I came straight to see Dr Bek.”</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Dr Bek, with white hair, is 67 years old. “Age isn’t a problem. Nothing can stop me <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;10&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> continuing to work here as long as I can,” he said.</span></p></div>",
