    "passage": "Eva, a middle school student, used to be a little lazy. She isn’t good at study. Last term, while she was watching a Chinese clothing show on TV, a kind of traditional clothes ___1___ hanfu caught her eyes. How she wished to have her own hanfu!\nOne day, ___2___ her way home from school, she told her mother that she wanted hanfu and said she became ___3___ in Chinese culture. Her mom thought for a while and said, “Darling, you can have one if you get good scores in the final exam.” After that, she studied much harder than before. She thought about giving up many times, because she found ___4___ difficult to make her dream come true. But she fought on. Eva tried her best to solve difficulties whenever she faced them. In class, she listened to the teachers carefully. After school, she finished homework correctly. Then, in the final exam, she made great ___5___ . And her mom was happy with her. Finally, the “big” day came. When she got home one afternoon, she saw ___6___ beautiful big box on the table: “Wow, hanfu! It ___7___ of silk. Thanks, mom!”\nNow, Eva is wearing her own hanfu to a park with her family. She is introducing hanfu to some foreign children ___8___ . She tells them hanfu is getting more and more popular in China. ___9___ beautiful the hanfu is in all the children’s eyes! She really enjoys the beauty of hanfu and experiences the Chinese traditional culture.\nLooking back at the past days, Eva thinks ___10___ she has got a lot more than the new clothes. Whenever she sees hanfu, it reminds her that hard work can help her get what she wants.",
    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\">Eva, a middle school student, used to be a little lazy. She isn’t good at study. Last term, while she was watching a Chinese clothing show on TV, a kind of traditional clothes <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;1&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> hanfu caught her eyes. How she wished to have her own hanfu!</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">One day, <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;2&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> her way home from school, she told her mother that she wanted hanfu and said she became <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;3&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> in Chinese culture. Her mom thought for a while and said, “Darling, you can have one if you get good scores in the final exam.” After that, she studied much harder than before. She thought about giving up many times, because she found <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;4&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> difficult to make her dream come true. But she fought on. Eva tried her best to solve difficulties whenever she faced them. In class, she listened to the teachers carefully. After school, she finished homework correctly. Then, in the final exam, she made great <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;5&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> . And her mom was happy with her. Finally, the “big” day came. When she got home one afternoon, she saw <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;6&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> beautiful big box on the table: “Wow, hanfu! It <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;7&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> of silk. Thanks, mom!”</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Now, Eva is wearing her own hanfu to a park with her family. She is introducing hanfu to some foreign children <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;8&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> . She tells them hanfu is getting more and more popular in China. <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;9&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> beautiful the hanfu is in all the children’s eyes! She really enjoys the beauty of hanfu and experiences the Chinese traditional culture.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">Looking back at the past days, Eva thinks <u>&nbsp;&nbsp;10&nbsp;&nbsp;</u> she has got a lot more than the new clothes. Whenever she sees hanfu, it reminds her that hard work can help her get what she wants.</span></p>",
