    "title": "九上阅读 · 三十一 中国2D动画电影《浪浪山的小妖怪",
    "passage": "A Chinese 2D animated film, “Nobody” (The Little Monsters of Langlang Mountain), has become a summer hit. Made by Shanghai Animation Film Studio, it was released (上映) on August 2nd, 2025. By August 11th, it had earned 574 million yuan, breaking the record for Chinese 2D animated films—Big Fish & Begonia’s (《大鱼海棠》) 573 million yuan. It also got 8.6 on Douban, winning the hearts of both kids and adults.\n\nThe film tells a warm story. Based on a short film from Chinese Tales, it follows four little monsters: a pig, a toad (蟾蜍), a weasel (黄鼠狼), and a gorilla. They work for a mountain king, but lose their jobs by accident. To survive, they pretend (假扮) to be Tang Monk and his team from Journey to the West (a famous Chinese classic) and start a journey west. Along the way, they grow from finding food to saving villagers. A famous line says, “We may be nobodies in society, but we are pillars (顶梁柱) at home,” making people think about life.\n\nWhat makes it special? Its beautiful Chinese ink painting style stands out—each picture uses 50 ink layers. The name of the movie is also very meaningful and profound (具有深意的). “Nobody” tells us: even small people can be heroes.\n\nThe film’s success has also made its merchandise (商品) popular. Over 300 products, from plush toys to stationery, sell quickly.\n\n“Nobody” is more than a movie. It brings joy and teaches us that everyone can be a hero.",
    "passageHtml": "<p><span class=\"ind\">A Chinese 2D animated film, “Nobody” (The Little Monsters of Langlang Mountain), has become a summer hit. Made by Shanghai Animation Film Studio, it was released (上映) on August 2nd, 2025. By August 11th, it had earned 574 million yuan, breaking the record for Chinese 2D animated films—Big Fish &amp; Begonia’s (《大鱼海棠》) 573 million yuan. It also got 8.6 on Douban, winning the hearts of both kids and adults.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">The film tells a warm story. Based on a short film from Chinese Tales, it follows four little monsters: a pig, a toad (蟾蜍), a weasel (黄鼠狼), and a gorilla. They work for a mountain king, but lose their jobs by accident. To survive, they pretend (假扮) to be Tang Monk and his team from Journey to the West (a famous Chinese classic) and start a journey west. Along the way, they grow from finding food to saving villagers. A famous line says, “We may be nobodies in society, but we are pillars (顶梁柱) at home,” making people think about life.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">What makes it special? Its beautiful Chinese ink painting style <u>stands out</u>—each picture uses 50 ink layers. The name of the movie is also very meaningful and profound (具有深意的). “Nobody” tells us: even small people can be heroes.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">The film’s success has also made its merchandise (商品) popular. Over 300 products, from plush toys to stationery, sell quickly.</span></p><p><span class=\"ind\">“Nobody” is more than a movie. It brings joy and teaches us that everyone can be a hero.</span></p>",
    "intro": "本文介绍了中国2D动画电影《浪浪山的小妖怪》。",
